course: dictionary
lesson: 10632
title: Words for feelings and manners
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ungrateful means not thankful. It is what someone is when they do not show thanks after being helped or given something. The start of the word, un-, means not, so ungrateful is the opposite of grateful.
explain: «I am very sorry indeed for my foolish and ungrateful conduct» is an apology. The speaker is saying sorry for behaving in a way that did not show thanks. The word sorry is a clue that ungrateful is something bad that was done.
explain: «Then a second feeling came on top: guilt for being ungrateful, because her parents had tried.» The girl feels guilty because her parents made an effort and she did not show thanks. Guilt is a clue that ungrateful is not a good way to behave. Check your meaning by swapping in not thankful: it still makes sense.
fact: Ungrateful means not thankful, not showing thanks for help or a gift.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so ungrateful is the opposite of grateful.
fact: Other un- words follow the same pattern: unhappy means not happy, and unkind means not kind.
fact: «Ungrateful» is often used for someone who does not say thank you or who complains about a present.
fact: Context clues such as «sorry» and «guilt» show that ungrateful describes behaviour that people feel bad about.
exercise: «I am very sorry indeed for my foolish and ungrateful conduct.» What does ungrateful mean here? | Very tired | Loud and cheerful | *Not thankful | Very kind
exercise: Which part of ungrateful tells you it means not? | The whole word has no clues | The middle letters, -grat- | The -ful at the end | *The un- at the start
exercise: Mum says, «Don't be ungrateful!» when Sam moans about his birthday present. What does she mean? | Don't be late for tea | Don't open your present yet | *Don't forget to say thank you for a gift | Don't sing in the car
test: She was ___ and forgot to say thank you for the lovely meal. | *ungrateful | hopeful | playful
test: What is the opposite of ungrateful? | *Grateful | Greedy | Gloomy
exam: The girl felt guilty for being ungrateful, because her parents had tried. Why did she feel guilty? | Her parents were angry about the cost | She had been too thankful | *She had not shown thanks for her parents' effort | She had lost her hamster
